{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block body %}
<section class="hero">
  <h1>Installers for your software, from a readable script</h1>
  <p class="lead">Write what to install in a few lines of YAML: where to download the newest version, the pictures and the
    license to show, the folder, the shortcuts. Your users get one small executable (Windows, macOS, Linux) that installs
    the newest version, with an uninstaller.</p>
  <p><a class="button primary" href="{{ path('login') }}">Sign in</a>
     <a class="button" href="https://github.com/davidnurdin/jumphp2installer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The project</a></p>
</section>
<section class="cards">
  <div class="card"><h2>A script anyone can read</h2>
<pre class="code">app: {name: My App, banner: banner.png}
version: {github: me/myapp}
pages: [welcome, folder, install, finish]
steps:
  - download: https://github.com/me/myapp/releases/latest/download/myapp-{platform}.zip
  - extract
  - shortcut: {target: "{folder}/myapp{exe}"}
  - uninstaller</pre></div>
  <div class="card"><h2>One installer, its id in its name</h2><p>Each download is the same installer, with this
    server's address and the package's id written in: <code>My-App-setup-k2q9x7a1.exe</code>. It always installs the
    newest version: no installer to rebuild when you release.</p></div>
  <div class="card"><h2>No server? GitHub</h2><p>The same package can live in your GitHub releases, installers included:
    <code>tools/github-release.sh</code> or the <code>package</code> workflow.</p></div>
</section>
<p class="muted center">Installers on this server: {{ platforms ? platforms|join(', ') : 'none yet (bin/console app:installers:fetch)' }}</p>
{% endblock %}
